<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sanford B. Dole</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1844–1926</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sanford Ballard Dole</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sanford B. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dole">Dole</a> was a Hawaiian-born lawyer of American missionary parents who led the government formed after the overthrow of Queen Liliuokalani in 1893. He was president of the Provisional Government and from 1894 of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a>, pressing for annexation by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, achieved in 1898, and became the first governor of the Territory of Hawaii in 1900.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sanford-b-dole.jpg" alt="Sanford B. Dole" width="320" height="369" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sanford_B._Dole_holding_newspaper.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
